{{!
    @template tool_vae/source_code

    The code of a certification record in bold, then its provenance line when it has one, with nothing between them: a
    cell of a table of the administration screen.

    Every text comes from the context, given by tool_vae\output\source_code. The template holds no logic. The code is
    escaped (double braces). One key is HTML (triple braces): provenancehtml, drawn by the template tool_vae/provenance,
    which escapes its sentence.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * code - string, the code of the record
    * provenancehtml - false, or HTML: the provenance line

    Example context (json):
    {
        "code": "RNCP36832",
        "provenancehtml": "<div class=\"small text-muted\">Source: France compétences, Licence Ouverte 2.0.</div>"
    }
}}
<strong>{{code}}</strong>{{#provenancehtml}}{{{provenancehtml}}}{{/provenancehtml}}
